{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2021 Fall AMC 10B #2</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2021 Fall AMC 12B #2</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Area_Addition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Area Addition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Area_Subtraction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Area Subtraction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Shoelace_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Shoelace Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Pick&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Pick's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of the shaded figure shown below?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/950ff8f5847f0f8acb13a489295e0c08395cb448.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.4)+fontsize(12)); pen s = linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(8);  pair O,X,Y; O = origin; X = (6,0); Y = (0,5); fill((1,0)--(3,5)--(5,0)--(3,2)--cycle, palegray+opacity(0.2)); for (int i=1; i&lt;7; ++i) { draw((i,0)--(i,5), gray+dashed); label(&quot;${&quot;+string(i)+&quot;}$&quot;, (i,0), 2*S); if (i&lt;6) { draw((0,i)--(6,i), gray+dashed); label(&quot;${&quot;+string(i)+&quot;}$&quot;, (0,i), 2*W); } } label(&quot;$0$&quot;, O, 2*SW); draw(O--X+(0.35,0), black+1.5, EndArrow(10)); draw(O--Y+(0,0.35), black+1.5, EndArrow(10)); draw((1,0)--(3,5)--(5,0)--(3,2)--(1,0), black+1.5); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"288\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a85acb2efa4efd568e3168d3f7d8ef18af621a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\: 4\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} \\: 6\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} \\: 8\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} \\: 10\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} \\: 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"362\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Area_Addition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Area_Addition)\">Solution 1 (Area Addition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Area Addition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line of symmetry divides the shaded figure into two congruent triangles, each with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the area of the shaded figure is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d4bdf0660f7ecc1c8db029d77a71a94d5925fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\cdot\\left(\\frac12\\cdot3\\cdot2\\right)=2\\cdot3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\: 6}.\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"43\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM ~Wilhelm Z\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Area_Subtraction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Area_Subtraction)\">Solution 2 (Area Subtraction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Area Subtraction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the area of the shaded figure, we subtract the area of the smaller triangle (base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) from the area of the larger triangle (base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />): <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f4549488e5575113e4bc3c0ded44f9db3c88a1f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12\\cdot4\\cdot5-\\frac12\\cdot4\\cdot2=10-4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\: 6}.\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"37\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM ~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com) \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Shoelace_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Shoelace_Theorem)\">Solution 3 (Shoelace Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Shoelace Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The consecutive vertices of the shaded figure are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a3d56e4ea1f4d719525391414018c001718fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0),(3,2),(5,0),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b9a4affce29dd3c35d71f78d262d8f160f8f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,5).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a>, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/62964fd1a93ce6cac7270ea14e2167c9365cd3aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12\\cdot|(1\\cdot2+3\\cdot0+5\\cdot5+3\\cdot0)-(0\\cdot3+2\\cdot5+0\\cdot3+5\\cdot1)|=\\frac12\\cdot12=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\: 6}.\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"37\" />\n~Taco12 ~I-AM-DA-KING\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Pick.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Pick's_Theorem)\">Solution 4 (Pick's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Pick&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lattice points in the interior and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lattice points on the boundary. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pick%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Pick&#39;s Theorem\">Pick's Theorem</a>, the area of the shaded figure is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/81411734430f77e31c966a110c816c2ef4d4b3fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4+\\frac{6}{2}-1 = 4+3-1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\: 6}.\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"37\" />\n~danprathab\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p9_RH4s-kBA?t=110\">https://youtu.be/p9_RH4s-kBA?t=110</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZV-cQm5p7Pc\">https://youtu.be/ZV-cQm5p7Pc</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1sAevgxImQM\">https://youtu.be/1sAevgxImQM</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For AMC 10: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/lC7naDZ1Eu4?t=512\">https://youtu.be/lC7naDZ1Eu4?t=512</a>\n</p><p>For AMC 12: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yaE5aAmeesc?t=512\">https://youtu.be/yaE5aAmeesc?t=512</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/P